Description: doc: serialize the three doxygen runs (parallel-make race)
 The doc target depends on three independent add_custom_command rules
 (Doxyfile html, Doxyfile-1 man1, Doxyfile-5 man5) that each run
 doxygen writing under the shared doc output tree.  Under a parallel
 make (dpkg default -jN; -j48 on the Athena builder) they run
 concurrently and race creating the shared output directories —
 doxygen 1.9.4 aborts:
 .
   error: Could not create output directory
   .../obj-x86_64-linux-gnu/doc/man
   make[3]: *** [doc/CMakeFiles/doc.dir/build.make:91:
   doc/man/man5/editorconfig-format.5] Error 1
 .
 Chain the commands (man1 after html, man5 after man1) so the three
 doxygen invocations serialize; doc generation is a trivial fraction
 of the build so the lost parallelism is irrelevant.
Origin: vendor, Athena-Build
Forwarded: no
Author: Athena-Build
Last-Update: 2026-11-08
---
--- a/doc/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/doc/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -76,6 +76,11 @@
             ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/Doxyfile.in
             DEPENDS
             ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/include/editorconfig/editorconfig.h
+            # Serialize after the main doxygen run: concurrent doxygen
+            # instances race creating the shared output directories under
+            # a parallel make and abort with "Could not create output
+            # directory" (seen at -j48).
+            ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/html/index.html
             WORKING_DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR})
 
         # Generating man page editorconfig-format.5. Although we have other
@@ -93,6 +98,8 @@
             ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/Doxyfile.in
             DEPENDS
             ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/include/editorconfig/editorconfig.h
+            # Serialize after the man1 doxygen run (see above).
+            ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/man/man1/editorconfig.1
             WORKING_DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR})
 
         # doc generation target
